# TEMPLATE ONLY for /opt/beebase/config/statistics.env -
# statistics-service's own production configuration. Never loaded by
# deploy.sh, Docker Compose, or the app directly (see
# docker-compose.prod.yml's env_file: entry for the `statistics-service`
# service, which reads the REAL file this template produces). Provision
# once on the EC2 host:
#   cp deploy/env-templates/statistics.env.example /opt/beebase/config/statistics.env
#   chmod 600 /opt/beebase/config/statistics.env
#
# statistics-service holds no database of its own - it computes every
# statistic fresh, on every request, from the other BeeBase services. Its
# network topology is supplied by docker-compose.prod.yml's `environment:`
# block. INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN is the existing shared internal-service
# credential and is supplied there as well; it must match the token already
# used by inspection-service and the other internal callers. Never place the
# real token in this template or in Git.
#
# This file still has to exist - and be mode 0600 - because the Compose
# env_file: entry requires it and deploy.sh validates every service file.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logging (Optional)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Defaults to info when omitted.
# debug | info | warn | error (defaults to info if omitted)
#LOG_LEVEL=info
